{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780940814,"nonce":"Lbschmi0BjFYQuKMsPZQzAF6JWk=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABExcrzQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/237","origin":"github"},"title":"Add Garmin GCV-20 sidescan TF frames to BizzyBoat URDF","message":"## Problem\n\nThe `garmin_sidescan` driver (`sidescan_launch.py`) stamps its per-channel\n`RawSonarImage` messages with `bizzy/garmin_sidescan(_port/_starboard/_down)`\nframe IDs, but **BizzyBoat's URDF defines no such frames**.\n\nThe frames were mistakenly added to `ben_description` (BEN's URDF) in\n[rolker/ben_description#14](https://github.com/rolker/ben_description/pull/14)\n(closing ben_description#13). BizzyBoat neither includes nor depends on\n`ben_description`, and BEN's `robot_state_publisher` does not run on bizzy —\nso those frames never resolve in bizzy's TF tree. `ben_description` is the URDF\nfor BEN (Bathymetric Explorer and Navigator), a different vessel that does not\ncarry this sensor.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd the Garmin GCV-20 sidescan TF frames to BizzyBoat's own URDF:\n\n- New `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro` (`garmin_sidescan`\n  macro), following bizzy's URDF conventions (`bizzy/` prefix, `parent` param) —\n  not the `ben_`-prefixed/`namespace`-based ben_description style.\n- Include + instantiate it in `bizzyboat.urdf.xacro`, anchored to\n  `bizzy/base_link`: centered, ~0.15 m forward, against the hull underside.\n- Fix the now-stale comment in `sidescan_launch.py` that points at ben_description.\n\n## Companion\n\nRevert of the misplaced frames in BEN: rolker/ben_description (revert of #14).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}